===Etymology===
{{etymon|en|id=fruit|bor|es>guayaba>fruit|tree=1}}
Recorded since 1555, from {{bor|en|es|guayaba}}, from {{der|en|tnq|*wayaba}}.<ref>{{R:LPCA|113}}</ref> {{doublet|en|guayaba}}, which is now rare or obsolete.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɡwɑːvə/|a=US}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-guava.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɑːvə|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# A tropical [[tree]] or [[shrub]] of the [[myrtle]] family, {{taxfmt|Psidium guajava|species}}.
# Its yellowish [[tropical]] [[fruit]], 3 to 5 cm ({{frac|1|1|4}} to 2 inches), [[globular]] or [[pear]]-shaped with thin, yellow, green or brown [[skin]], is often made into [[jam]]s and [[jelly|jellies]]. The [[meat]]  can be yellowish to pale green or pink in color, depending on the variety.
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Eva Greene Fuller|passage=''CREAM CHEESE AND GUAVA JELLY SANDWICH'': Spread an equal number of slices of lightly buttered white bread with '''guava''' jelly and cream cheese. Put slices together and trim the edges.|page=118|title=[https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Page:The_Up-to-Date_Sandwich_Book.djvu/124 The Up-To-Date Sandwich Book: 400 Ways to Make a Sandwich]|publisher=|year=1909}}
# A medium [[red]]dish-pink [[colour]], like that of guava flesh (also called guava pink).
#: {{color panel|DF816B}}

